# Wire UC metric views into Ontology Generate

Context: After loading Unity Catalog metric views, Ontology → Generate
detection returned no entities. Mapping already treated metric views as
first-class sources; Stage 1 did not (metadata tools stripped object_kind
and column roles, the prompt treated sources as flat tables, and the
SELECT-permission probe used SELECT * which metric views reject).

Changes:

1. `src/agents/tools/metadata.py`
   `get_metadata` / `get_table_detail` expose `object_kind` and per-column
   `role`.
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py`
   Stage-1 prompt: metric-view dimensions are entity evidence; measures
   are never classes.
3. `src/back/core/databricks/uc/UnityCatalog.py`
   SELECT probe for metric views uses `build_metric_view_base_sql` + LIMIT 0.
4. `src/back/core/databricks/uc/MetadataService.py`,
   `src/back/core/databricks/DatabricksClient.py`,
   `src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py`,
   `src/back/objects/domain/_metadata_tasks.py`
   Load/refresh pass object_kind + columns into the probe; schema-wide
   probe skips metric views so SELECT * does not false-fail the picker.
5. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js`,
   `src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_wizard.html`
   Generate source list badges metric views.
6. `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md`,
   `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/metric_view.jsonl`
   Eval delta (10 rows) + SPEC tool/failure-mode notes. Live MLflow eval
   not run (warehouse + Foundation Model access).
7. `docs/features.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`
   Generate reads metric-view dimensions as entities.

